,"contentHtml":"\u003Cp\u003EI cannot seem to get the latest DeoVR app to use the \/deovr file like previous versions did half a year ago. I have checked the server logs and I see the quest 3 headset making calls to the main domain without the \/deovr like what\u0027s mentioned in the json documentation. I have been unable to have the DeoVR app switch from the web browsers to the deovr json file gui in headset. \u003Cbr\u003E\nI also see that the app and docs were updated when passthrough was supported so Im guessing even though the deovr app lists the json files as legacy it should still be supported.\u003C\/p\u003E\n\n\u003Cp\u003EI does not appear t support the deovr json files at all now and I cannot figure out how to make the deovr browser switch into the webxr view for my site.\u003C\/p\u003E\n\n\u003Cp\u003EI have tried using the deovr:\/\/https:\/\/....\/deovr too and that does not work either and my server has a valid ssl certificate.\u003C\/p\u003E\n\n\u003Cp\u003EThis was all working a year ago without any changes on my side except updating the deovr video player app on my quest 2 and same issue occurs with the quest 3.\u003C\/p\u003E\n\n\u003Cp\u003EIf deovr app does not support the legacy \/deovr json files anymore, how do I setup my vr site to utilize the deovr app or have you abandoned third party use since your expanding the deovr.com video hosting service?\u003C\/p\u003E","renderFailed":false,"canEdit":false,"canDelete":false,"canHide":false,"mentionedByCount":0,"canFlag":false,"isApproved":true,"canApprove":false,"canStartPoll":false,"canLike":false,"likesCount":0},"relationships":{"discussion":{"data":{"type":"discussions","id":"2659"}},"user":{"data":{"type":"users","id":"3639"}},"polls":{"data":[]},"mentionedBy":{"data":[]},"likes":{"data":[]}}},{"type":"posts","id":"6216","attributes":{"number":2,"createdAt":"2024-02-12T18:03:21+00:00","contentType":"comment","contentHtml":"\u003Cp\u003EHi, could you please post full links (URL) that you are tr